  "description": "BEMPAL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C19 H35 Ce1 Mn6 O30 1+,Cl1 O4 1-,0.5(C2 H4 O2),3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.706-3.373 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.28-128.67°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CeMn6O9(O2CMe)9(MeOH)(H2O)2](ClO4)·3H2O·1/2MeCO2H. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Mn(IV).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
